# Mission plan

**Execution model:** Squad Leader inventories GitHub vulnerability alerts with **`gh`**, triages recommended fixes with the developer, applies (or plans) lockfile/code patches using **`app/backend/README.md`** and **`app/frontend/README.md`** vulnerability sections, then reuses plan-and-deliver **`new-plan`** / **`pr-plan`** / **`coding-session`** for hosting-repo ship when product changes are required. **Forbidden:** inventing patch procedures that contradict those READMEs; Squad Leader proposing dispatch resolution without documenting residual open alerts in scope.

**Skill reuse:** [`.sedea/centers/research-and-development/missions/plan-and-deliver/skills/`](.sedea/centers/research-and-development/missions/plan-and-deliver/skills/) — **`new-plan`**, **`pr-plan`**, **`coding-session`**, **`pr-review`**. Spawn contracts: [`.sedea/centers/research-and-development/missions/plan-and-deliver/skills/README.md`](.sedea/centers/research-and-development/missions/plan-and-deliver/skills/README.md). Low-complexity single-PR patches may follow [quick-fix](.sedea/centers/research-and-development/missions/quick-fix/plan.mdc) constraints (complexity ≤6) when the developer confirms.

## Mission constraints (binding)

| Constraint | Rule |
|------------|------|
| **Inventory source** | Prefer **`gh`** (`gh api` / Dependabot / code-scanning / advisory surfaces available to the authenticated user) over manual guesswork |
| **Patch procedures** | Backend transitive lock patches: [`app/backend/README.md`](../../../../../app/backend/README.md) § *Vulnerability patches of transitive dependency directly in poetry.lock*. Frontend yarn.lock patches: [`app/frontend/README.md`](../../../../../app/frontend/README.md) § *Vulnerability version patches directly in yarn.lock* |
| **Target apps** | Vulnerability inventory and remediation target GitHub repos **`safebeat/app`** and **`safebeat/ucsf-study` only**. **Forbidden:** treating the Sedea hosting repo (`safebeat-sedea/sedea-app` or this workspace’s **`HOSTING_ROOT`**) as an inventory or remediation target. Within each product repo, resolve backend/frontend (Poetry/Yarn) paths from **that** repo’s layout — not hosting-repo `app/` paths. Narrow to a single repo only when the opening message or triage pick names one. |
| **Host shell** | Mission Control Shell has **no Python** — run Poetry/Yarn via documented host tooling or interactive terminal presets when credentials/interactive auth are required; do not invent `python3` workflows |
| **Ship chain** | Product lockfile/code changes ship via detached **`coding-session`** (same order as plan-and-deliver §8) — do not duplicate ship-chain steps here |
| **Out of scope** | Rewriting Sedea center governance; closing GitHub alerts without verifying the fix; force-ignoring alerts without documented deferral |

