Detached **`coding-session`** ship chains reuse plan-and-deliver mechanics. After **`create-pr`**, the inline **`pr-review`** boundary from [plan-and-deliver/plan.mdc § Post-PR handoff](.sedea/centers/research-and-development/missions/plan-and-deliver/plan.mdc) applies. When the developer picks **`start-pr-review`**, load [plan-and-deliver `pr-review/SKILL.md`](.sedea/centers/research-and-development/missions/plan-and-deliver/skills/pr-review/SKILL.md).

## Objectives

1. **Inventory** — Using **`gh`**, list open vulnerability alerts (Dependabot, security advisories, and/or code scanning as available) for the scoped GitHub repo(s), including recommended fix versions when GitHub supplies them.
2. **Triage** — With the developer, classify each in-scope alert: apply now, defer, or out-of-scope; record package ecosystem (Poetry backend vs Yarn frontend) and target path under the monorepo.
3. **Remediate** — Apply approved patches following the backend/frontend README vulnerability procedures; for multi-file or higher-complexity work, plan and ship via **`new-plan`** → **`pr-plan`** → **`coding-session`**.
4. **Verify and close** — Re-check alert status with **`gh`** after merge (or document residual risk); Squad Leader proposes dispatch resolution when in-scope items are fixed or explicitly deferred.

